The Mac cursor no longer shows over a game that hides it: a hidden Windows cursor is a transparent Mac cursor.

From Wine merge request 11880 (https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11880, LGPL-2.1-or-later),
"winemac: replace hidden cursor with transparent cursor" by Elvin Hayatov, version 2, head
6af3a97e71c8d5cd0e6a0c94b4e952fc60868718 (pushed 2026-10-08). Not merged in Wine as of 2026-10-23; carried until the
pinned sources include it. The changed lines are the merge request's, unchanged. Only one hunk's trailing context
differs: in the CrossOver 26.3.0 tree, -applicationDidBecomeActive: is followed by
-applicationDidChangeScreenParameters:, not -applicationDidResignActive:, so the context is regenerated against this
tree and the patch applies with no fuzz.

Why mavrik needs it: Wine's Mac driver hid the cursor with [NSCursor hide] once and then trusted its own flag.
macOS shows the cursor again on its own (after another app was in front, at the Dock edge, and when shake to locate
enlarges it), and Wine never hid it again, so the Mac cursor stayed over a full-screen game (Skyrim SE, mavrik S210;
Hadron issue 85 with Ready or Not). A transparent cursor leaves macOS nothing to undo; it is set again whenever
AppKit's current cursor differs and on every activation, and shake to locate is off only while a hidden or custom
cursor is active. Reading: mavrik .factory/design-passes/2026-10-23-s211/cursor.md.

The merge request's own commit follows.

From: Elvin Hayatov <AlvinHV@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 21:39:30 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: replace hidden cursor with transparent cursor

Native cursor hiding can make mouse movement block frame presentation until the display refresh interval, even when the game disables vertical synchronization. Cursor Location Assistance can trigger the same behavior.

Use a transparent NSCursor for Windows hidden-cursor requests and restore it when AppKit resets the current cursor. Disable Cursor Location Assistance only while a hidden or custom Windows cursor is active, following the approach used by Apple's Game Porting Toolkit guidance.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.h b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.h
index f9acd289..46fb9cf5 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.h
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.h
@@ -81,7 +81,6 @@ @interface WineApplicationController : NSObject <NSApplicationDelegate>
     NSTimer*    cursorTimer;
     NSCursor*   cursor;
     BOOL        cursorIsCurrent;
-    BOOL        cursorHidden;
     BOOL        clientWantsCursorHidden;
 
     NSTimeInterval lastSetCursorPositionTime;
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
index 0f6a0875..ee079d3f 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -131,6 +131,21 @@ static void set_display_name(NSString* name)
 }
 
 
+static NSCursor* WineTransparentCursor(void)
+{
+    static NSCursor* transparentCursor;
+    static dispatch_once_t once;
+
+    dispatch_once(&once, ^{
+        NSImage* image = [[NSImage alloc] initWithSize:NSMakeSize(1, 1)];
+        transparentCursor = [[NSCursor alloc] initWithImage:image hotSpot:NSZeroPoint];
+        [image release];
+    });
+
+    return transparentCursor;
+}
+
+
 @implementation WineApplication
 
 @synthesize wineController;
@@ -1095,22 +1110,18 @@ - (void) updateCursor:(BOOL)force
     {
         if (force || lastTargetWindow)
         {
-            if (clientWantsCursorHidden && !cursorHidden)
-            {
-                [NSCursor hide];
-                cursorHidden = TRUE;
-            }
+            NSCursor* desiredCursor = clientWantsCursorHidden ? WineTransparentCursor() : cursor;
+            BOOL cursorWasReset = desiredCursor && [NSCursor currentCursor] != desiredCursor;
 
-            if (!cursorIsCurrent)
+            if (force || !cursorIsCurrent || cursorWasReset)
             {
-                [cursor set];
+                [desiredCursor set];
                 cursorIsCurrent = TRUE;
-            }
 
-            if (!clientWantsCursorHidden && cursorHidden)
-            {
-                [NSCursor unhide];
-                cursorHidden = FALSE;
+                if (clientWantsCursorHidden || [cursorFrames count])
+                    NSApp.presentationOptions |= NSApplicationPresentationDisableCursorLocationAssistance;
+                else
+                    NSApp.presentationOptions &= ~NSApplicationPresentationDisableCursorLocationAssistance;
             }
         }
         else
@@ -1119,11 +1130,7 @@ - (void) updateCursor:(BOOL)force
             {
                 [[NSCursor arrowCursor] set];
                 cursorIsCurrent = FALSE;
-            }
-            if (cursorHidden)
-            {
-                [NSCursor unhide];
-                cursorHidden = FALSE;
+                NSApp.presentationOptions &= ~NSApplicationPresentationDisableCursorLocationAssistance;
             }
         }
     }
@@ -2517,6 +2524,10 @@ - (void)applicationDidBecomeActive:(NSNotification *)notification
         // movement deltas are invalidated.  Make sure the next mouse move event
         // starts over from an absolute baseline.
         forceNextMouseMoveAbsolute = TRUE;
+
+        // macOS may restore its cursor while another application is active.
+        // Reapply the cursor requested by the Windows application on activation.
+        [self updateCursor:TRUE];
     }
 
     - (void)applicationDidChangeScreenParameters:(NSNotification *)notification
